A||||3||Homicidal||Radio stations only get staticy when DRIVING?||||5||
Z||000000||Homicidal||06-26-2000||10:09 PM||||Not Fiero related, not even my car, but my sister has this problem.<P>She says her radio stations are staticy when driving.  I looked at her stereo, but I cannot see the antenna wire without taking the whole kit out.  Other than that, everything is fine.  What could cause this? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||06-26-2000||10:23 PM||||AM or FM?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Homicidal||06-26-2000||11:46 PM||||FM||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||06-28-2000||09:12 AM||||Make sure the antenna is screwed on tight. The rod can come loose from the mount. <BR>Look at the metal plate that's on the bottom of the decklid, just above the engine. There should be a ground wire connected to it. If it's an 88, the plate is actually part of the lid, but it still has the ground wire. <BR>If the FM is full of static, the AM will probably be useless. ||||reg||1
